       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum metformin dose. The labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, usually given as 850 mg three times daily. A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the typical 1,000 mg maximum per dose. Doses this high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWas this a typo? Some possibilities:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg** per dose, with a different frequency\n\nTell me the dose you intend and I'll enter it. If you really do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that and give the clinical rationale. I would still suggest checking with pharmacy first."
